course: dictionary
lesson: 4442
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to use. Handsome usually means good-looking, as when we say a boy is handsome. «The handsome prince rode into the story on a white horse.» The clue is that a prince is a person, so handsome means good-looking here.
explain: Look at what the word describes. «Alice sets the pig down and says it makes rather a handsome pig.» A pig is an animal, not a person, so handsome means fine and attractive to look at. Test it: swap in good-looking and it sounds odd for a pig, so pleasing to look at fits better.
explain: The third meaning is about size and generosity. «A handsome reward» and «a handsome win» show something large, not a face. When handsome sits next to money, a reward, a profit or a win, it usually means a large amount.
fact: Handsome means good-looking, usually said about a man or boy.
fact: A handsome animal, building or object is fine and attractive to look at.
fact: A handsome amount is large and generous, as in «a handsome reward», «a handsome profit» or «a handsome win».
fact: The adverb is handsomely, and the comparative forms are handsomer and handsomest.
fact: Context tells you which meaning to use: a person, a thing, or an amount.
exercise: «The handsome prince rode into the story on a white horse.» What does handsome mean here? | Large and generous | *Good-looking, describing a person | Fine to look at, like a building | Very old
exercise: Alice says the pig «makes rather a handsome pig». What does handsome mean? | Very quick | A large amount of money | Good-looking, used of a boy | *Fine and attractive to look at
exercise: «The team won a handsome victory.» What does handsome suggest? | A shy, quiet win | A win that was not fair | *A large, generous win | A win by a single point
test: «She was given a handsome reward for finding the lost dog.» Which meaning fits handsome here? | Fine to look at, like a house | Good-looking, about a man | Old and ancient | *Large and generous
test: Which word is the adverb form of handsome? | *handsomely | handsomer | handsomeness | handsomest
exam: Mum says, «The gardener was handsomely paid for the work.» What does handsomely mean? | Good-looking | Quietly and slowly | Fine to look at | *Generously, with a large amount
